# Routine Manager — build rules

## Source of truth

- Follow `IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md` strictly (user stories, architecture, schemas, and feature specs).
- Implement **one atomic feature at a time** in checklist order.
- **Do not start Feature N+1** until Feature N’s acceptance tests pass and the user confirms it works (or the feature’s DONE criteria are met).
- When asked “what next?”, answer with the **first unchecked** feature in the master checklist — never jump ahead to calendar, AI, or deploy features.

## Security

- OpenAI API keys and other secrets stay on the **backend only** (env vars / host dashboard).
- Never put secrets in the mobile app, `EXPO_PUBLIC_*` vars, commits, or client bundles.
- Commit `.env.example` only; never commit `.env`.

## Stack conventions

- Mobile: Expo + Expo Router (file-based routing) + TypeScript.
- Backend: Node.js + Express + MongoDB/Mongoose + OpenAI tool calling.
- Prefer Expo docs / installed project skills (`expo-router`, `eas-update`, `vercel-react-native-skills`, etc.).
- Android-first testing; keep iOS permissions and config ready for later publishing.

## Teaching

- The user is new to mobile development. When implementing, briefly explain mobile-specific concepts (Expo Go vs dev builds, Metro, EAS Update, notifications, etc.) in plain language — short, not lecture-length.
